      "## Concurrency as a built-in\n\nA **goroutine** is a lightweight function execution started with `go f()`; thousands can run cheaply. **Channels** pass values between goroutines safely: `ch <- v` sends and `v := <-ch` receives. The Go proverb: *share memory by communicating*.\n\nUse `sync.WaitGroup` to wait for goroutines, `select` to wait on several channels, and `context.Context` to cancel work. Beware leaking goroutines that block forever on a channel nobody reads.",
